      "writtenOn": "2021-06-02T16:32:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is catching a real issue... how do we know that the flag you defined for this feature isn\u0027t used for something else if the value isn\u0027t reserved anywhere?\n\nIf you need a new flag for your private use, I think it would be better to define something like \n```\n#define WF_VENDOR 0x1000\n```\nin kernel/sched/sched.h and then change this line to\n```\nWARN_ON_ONCE(IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SCHED_DEBUG) \u0026\u0026 wake_flags \u0026 ~(WF_SYNC|WF_VENDOR));\n```",
      "parentUuid": "f53249d7_8a1aec3f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5019,
        "startChar": 26,
